# GitHub operations via MCP (OBRA_APP)

When interacting with **GitHub as a platform** (issues, pull requests, reviews, comments, repository metadata, search, remote file contents, branches/tags/releases, Copilot review requests, etc.), use the **`user-github` MCP server** tools.

## Do not use shell for GitHub API–style work

Avoid:

- `gh` CLI (e.g. `gh pr`, `gh issue`, `gh api`)
- `curl` / `wget` against `api.github.com` or GitHub REST/GraphQL
- Scripts whose main job is to read or change GitHub-hosted state outside local git objects

If the GitHub MCP lacks a needed capability, say so and ask how to proceed instead of falling back to bash.

## Local git is still fine

Ordinary **local** git in the repo (status, add, commit, rebase, merge, checkout) does not need MCP. Prefer MCP when the task is clearly **remote GitHub** (open/update PR, comment, list issues, merge, request review, search org repos, etc.).

## Quick mapping

| Intent | Use |
|--------|-----|
| Create/update PR, review, merge | GitHub MCP (`pull_request_*`, `merge_pull_request`, etc.) |
| Issues and comments | GitHub MCP (`issue_*`, `add_issue_comment`, etc.) |
| Read/write files on default branch | GitHub MCP (`get_file_contents`, `create_or_update_file`, etc.) or local git + push policy per project |
| Repo/search discovery | GitHub MCP (`search_*`, `list_*`, `get_*`) |
| Local commits and history | `git` in terminal |

```bash
# BAD — use GitHub MCP instead for PR/issue/API tasks
gh pr list
gh api repos/owner/repo/issues

# GOOD — local only
git status
git commit -m "fix: typo"
```
